From fd2c1041ba53300913b060818feffb23fecf3dd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 22:27:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03353/11362] [outer-loop] arc: goal-distance gradient built --
 recovers nav-tail but modest efficiency (near-0 score)

General avatar+goal detector -> Manhattan heuristic -> graph_explore_solve_v2 A*. Recovers ls20
(avatar=9, 15-action win) + tu93 (avatar=6, 18-action), correctly self-scopes su15 as not-a-nav-game
(no avatar), m0r0 detects avatar but goal-candidates miss. Efficiency: ls20 at ~1000-1500 expansions
vs blind BFS 1777 -- MODEST ~15-30%, not dramatic (the path reverses around obstacles so goal-descent
stalls onto the BFS depth term; the 4 rare-cell goal-candidates only approximate the true goal). So the
nav hard-tail is REACHABLE but not EFFICIENTLY: deep 13-18 action wins still cost ~1500 search expansions
-> near-0 efficiency score. The shipped diversity floor (4/11) remains the meaningful win; the hard
tail's efficient recovery is genuine frontier research. goal-distance is a working GENERAL toolkit
member for the feature-router (handles + self-scopes the nav class, transfers to hidden nav games).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
